From c811e97a00f39152b45cc9243a345c3ccf302541 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dev-jam <mail@bobrosbag.nl>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 11:18:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] update-repo.sh: keep Release out of its own checksum list

apt-ftparchive release lists every index file it finds under
dists/$SUITE, Release files included. The script wrote its output with
"> dists/$SUITE/Release", and the shell creates (and truncates) that
file before apt-ftparchive scans the directory. The previous Release
was therefore listed in itself, under MD5Sum, SHA1, SHA256 and SHA512,
with the checksum and size of whatever was there at scan time, which
does not match the final file.

Remove the old Release first and let apt-ftparchive write to
.cache/Release.new, outside dists/, then move it into place. Tested
with apt-ftparchive on a copy of dists/trixie: the old way gives 4
entries named Release, the new way none, also on a second run.

Release.gpg and InRelease were never listed, so their handling stays
the same.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 scripts/update-repo.sh | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/scripts/update-repo.sh b/scripts/update-repo.sh
index 72c441f..1b88cfd 100755
--- a/scripts/update-repo.sh
+++ b/scripts/update-repo.sh
@@ -65,7 +65,13 @@ echo
 
 # Generate and sign the Release files
 echo "Generating and signing Release files..."
-apt-ftparchive -c .cache/release.conf release "dists/$SUITE" > "dists/$SUITE/Release"
+# apt-ftparchive release lists every Release file it finds under dists/$SUITE,
+# so the old one must be gone and the new one written outside dists/; a plain
+# "> dists/$SUITE/Release" creates the file before the scan and Release then
+# lists itself with a wrong checksum
+rm -f "dists/$SUITE/Release"
+apt-ftparchive -c .cache/release.conf release "dists/$SUITE" > .cache/Release.new
+mv -f .cache/Release.new "dists/$SUITE/Release"
 gpg --yes --default-key "$KEY" -abs -o "dists/$SUITE/Release.gpg" "dists/$SUITE/Release"
 gpg --yes --default-key "$KEY" --clearsign -o "dists/$SUITE/InRelease" "dists/$SUITE/Release"
 echo
-- 
2.43.0

